# .secret-patterns.example
#
# Copy this file to .secret-patterns (which is git-ignored), then replace
# the placeholders. check-secrets.ps1 reads one .NET regex per line and
# ignores lines starting with '#'.
#
# Do NOT put real values in this example file - it ships in the repo.

# Your Windows user name, if it shows up in absolute paths.
# Replace <name> with the actual name. Do not keep the angle brackets.
#   ^C:\\Users\\<name>\\

# A phone number (mainland China format, adjust for your region).
#   \b1[3-9][0-9]{9}\b

# Your mailbox domain or address fragment, if you do not want it public.
#   @example\.com

# A project-internal hostname or token prefix.
#   internal-[a-z0-9]{8}

# NOTE: the copyright line in LICENSE carries your name on purpose.
# Do not put that name here, or LICENSE itself gets flagged as a leak.
